{
  "_comment": "Rename this file to targets.json and fill in your real values.",

  "vaults": [
    { "key": "eu", "name": "Bitwarden EU", "serverUrl": "https://vault.bitwarden.eu" },
    { "key": "com", "name": "Bitwarden US", "serverUrl": "https://vault.bitwarden.com" },
    { "key": "selfhosted", "name": "Self-hosted", "serverUrl": "https://bitwarden.example.internal", "logoutAfterImport": true }
  ],

  "backupFolder": "/backups",
  "bitwardenConfigDir": "/data",

  "_accounts_comment": [
    "One Bitwarden identity on ONE vault. The same person on two vaults is two accounts,",
    "and they do NOT have to share an email or a master password.",
    "otp: 'required' asks for the two-step code in the same prompt as the password.",
    "otp: 'unknown' (the default) does not mean the account has no two-step login — only that",
    "it is not recorded here, so the code is asked for in a second prompt if the CLI wants one.",
    "otpMethod: 0 = authenticator app, 1 = email, 3 = YubiKey.",
    "The key becomes a directory name under bitwardenConfigDir, so keep it simple."
  ],
  "accounts": [
    { "key": "alice@eu", "vault": "eu", "email": "alice@example.com", "displayName": "Alice", "otp": "required", "otpMethod": 0 },
    { "key": "alice@com", "vault": "com", "email": "alice.personal@example.com", "displayName": "Alice" },
    { "key": "bob@com", "vault": "com", "email": "bob@example.com", "displayName": "Bob" },
    { "key": "bob@selfhosted", "vault": "selfhosted", "email": "bob@example.internal", "displayName": "Bob" }
  ],

  "_orgs_comment": "An org's id differs per vault. List only the vaults it actually exists on.",
  "orgs": [
    {
      "key": "acme",
      "name": "Acme Corp",
      "ids": {
        "com": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
        "selfhosted": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002"
      }
    }
  ],

  "_syncs_comment": [
    "One directed route, and the unit everything is keyed on: the sync key names the job",
    "target, the backup files and the dashboard row. from/to are ACCOUNT keys, so each side",
    "brings its own email, password and vault. Omit 'org' for a personal-vault route.",
    "One source account can feed several routes (fan-out to more than one destination)."
  ],
  "syncs": [
    { "key": "alice", "from": "alice@eu", "to": "alice@com" },
    { "key": "bob", "from": "bob@com", "to": "bob@selfhosted" },
    { "key": "acme", "from": "bob@com", "to": "bob@selfhosted", "org": "acme" }
  ],

  "retention": {
    "keepDaily": 7,
    "keepMonthly": 12
  },

  "importGuard": {
    "minSourceRatio": 0.5,
    "blockOnEmptySource": true
  },

  "logoutAfterImport": true
}
